 "text": "You're probably putting your deodorant on at the wrong time. Here's why: pit stains by lunch, changing your shirt before a meeting, keeping your arms down in every photo. This is Carpe in Mountain Breeze. It's clinically tested for up to a hundred hours of sweat and odor control, but only if you use it right. When it's new, it looks empty, so just keep twisting. You only need a pea. Put it on at night on dry skin, let it dry, then again in the morning. Night is the step people miss. If sweat's never bothered you, scroll on. If it has, don't wait till holiday party photos. It's linked below.",
